this video is made possible by  Skillshare home to over 17,000 classes  that could help you learn a new life  skill be one of the first 500 to sign up  using the link below and get a two month  free trial with Skillshare judging by  the news and the state of world affairs  it's pretty easy to see why some people  think we may be nearing the end of the  world 10th political relations deep  societal divides rampant terrorist  activity and at least a handful of world  powers with access to huge numbers of  nuclear weapons does not bode well for  the future of humanity of course the  Cold War was as close as the world has  gotten to Armageddon and if we avoided  that perhaps we're not as doomed as we  might think that being said world  relations are about as frosty as they've  been since the Cold War especially with  the rumors of election meddling by the  Russian government and the bizarre  Twitter slap fight between Kim jong-un  and Donald Trump  so if society does collapse weather  thanks to nuclear fallout civil war or  some yet unknown Cataclysm how can we  make sure we're prepared in this  scenario we're going to assume that the  electrical grid has gone down which  means you won't be able to rely on your  electronics to survive however that  doesn't mean your cell phone will be  completely useless apps like backcountry  navigator for android and gaia gps for  iOS allow you to download maps to use  offline so even if you can't get Wi-Fi  or cell service any more  you can still figure out where you're  going your cell phone battery won't last  forever so make sure you have an  external power bank and a solar charger  to keep it operational just to be safe  keep a paper map of your area in your  backpack in case your phone breaks or  gets lost depending on the type of  apocalypse we're dealing with it might  be safest for you to remain in your home  for a few days use this time to gather  little necessities things like  prescription drugs allergy pills contact  lenses and extra glasses matches and  lighters to start fires flashlights and  extra pair of shoes layers of clothing a  can opener a multi-tool duct tape  paracord the list goes on and on  basically you need to grab everything  you can easily carry that will keep  tasks simple the most important things  you can gather from your home are things  you can put in a first-aid kit if you  don't have a pre-made one hydrogen  peroxide neosporin painkillers gauze  bandages tweezers and scissors an EpiPen  if you have one anything that could stop  a potential infection blood loss or  other medical emergency pack everything  you've gathered into the biggest  backpack you have  a camping or military bag works best  since they tend to have a large capacity  and lots of pockets but make do with  what you have have everything packed and  ready to leave at a moment's notice if  the grid is down then the only way  you'll be able to gather news from the  outside world is by using a radio having  a hand-cranked portable radio available  could be the difference between knowing  critical information and sitting in the  dark hoping for the best when you're  eventually forced to leave your home and  search for supplies you'll need a way to  collect safe drinking water there are a  few ways to do this first you can start  a fire and boil the water this should  clean it of most impurities but it does  take a while  second you can use a water purifier one  of the smallest and lightest options is  the LifeStraw it functions just like a  straw filtering water as it passes  through for larger groups there's also  the LifeStraw family which is a bigger  purifier you could set up at your  campsites but still small enough to  carry in a backpack finally if the  apocalypse you are dealing with is  caused by a virus you'll have to be very  careful with your drinking water for a  situation like that you'll want  something like the MSR Guardian filter  it does everything the LifeStraw  products do but it also filters out  viruses meaning you won't have to worry  about becoming a zombie after drinking  from that pond you found when you  eventually run out of canned and  dehydrated food you'll have to forage  and hunt to survive in the short term  and probably learn to farm if society  has truly crumbled beyond repair if  you're near a large body of water fish  are a nutritious and plentiful source of  food opt for a net instead of a fishing  rod to catch as many fish as you can in  a shorter amount of time  Nets also make decent traps for small  game and unwanted visitors for hunting  you have several options  first there's the bow quieter than  firearms a bow will let you hunt without  giving away your location to nearby  scavengers and makes a valuable ranged  weapon if they do find you on the other  hand bows do require more skill to use  effectively when hunting large game a  lot of people aren't comfortable  carrying a gun around or even owning one  but when the world falls apart and you  need a tool to protect yourself and your  loved ones from wild animals and in a  worst case scenario hostile humans it's  probably better to have one if you don't  have a rifle and you're an American  you're in luck because they're  ridiculously easy to buy especially if  you live somewhere like Texas that has  frequent gun shows this is a Mosin  Nagant a World War 2 era Russian  bolt-action rifle that was the most  widely produced gun in the world  until it was dethroned by the ak-47 that  means they can be had for next to  nothing and are available without a  license to just about anyone 18 or older  this is about 400 rounds of surplus  World War two steel core ammunition the  gun and the ammo together can easily be  found for about 200 to 300 dollars at  any decently sized gun show the only  things to consider when hunting with  this type of weapon and ammo is that  it's very loud and there might not be  anything left of the animal if it's  small like a rabbit so you might want to  use something like a slingshot to hunt  small game if you really don't want to  be put into a situation where you could  injure or kill another human being but  still want to scare people off at a  distance keep the gun unloaded or remove  the bolt and leave it in another bag  unless you intend to use it plants can  make a welcome addition to your diet but  many plants are toxic to humans so make  sure you have a hand guide to help you  determine what's edible and what's not  the last big consideration for surviving  the apocalypse is finding and  maintaining a good shelter tall highway  overpasses or bridges make for great  defensible locations if you can  barricade or destroy the ends you'll  just need a way to get down and hunt for  supplies large boats crewed by people  you trust could be another good option  if you have access to enough fuel to  last at least several weeks you could  sail out into deep water to isolate  yourself for most survivors but if  pirates come knocking you'll have to be  prepared to fight them off or give them  what they want two more options include  small uninhabited islands and offshore  oil rigs an island would be ideal for  survivors who hope to set up a permanent  settlement complete with small farms to  grow food on the other hand if you have  the supplies to last you a while and can  gain access to an oil rig  you've got possibly the best defensive  shelter you can find a pre-made metal  fortress raised high above the ocean  makes for an excellent base of  operations just make sure you have a  radio to know when it's safe to return  to dry land last but not least don't  discount the tried-and-true off-the-grid  cabin in the woods the United States  still has huge expanses of forests and  protected national parks which makes for  prime real estate for the experienced  woodsman if you have hunting and farming  know-how and can fashion a shelter out  in the middle of the woods then this  simple option could be your best bet  you'll have easy access to food in the  form of wild game and plants water from  streams plenty of material to build a  shelter and tools or weapons and enough  uninhabited land that you'll likely  never encounter another survivor as  scary as a post-apocalyptic world sounds  the good news is we're not  there yet and we may never be we have  the time to prepare and put together an  emergency kit just in case thanks to the  Internet there's a huge amount of  knowledge to be gained from experts in  the arts of hunting farming tracking and  general survival all it takes is a  little diligence to learn and prepare  for the worst best case scenario you  never have to use your newfound  knowledge and you get a bunch of useful  camping gear out of it  worst case scenario you'll be ready  while we're talking about learning a  great place to learn something new is  skill share as you all know I'm always  trying to improve my videos without  compromising the fun simple style we all  know and love to do that I'm taking a  class to polish my editing skills with  skill share learning by trial and error  is great but when you really want to  fast track your learning organize  classes are the way to go skill share is  an online learning community for  creators featuring over 17,000 classes  and video editing animation graphic  design film production and more anyone  can take a class try a project or even  teach a class themselves Premium  Membership begins around ten bucks a  month for unlimited access to everything  as a little thank you for watching my  videos skill share is offering a two  month free trial to the first 500 people  who sign up using the link below you can  use those two months to learn an awesome  new skill that you can use to market  yourself create a business or even start  a YouTube channel like I did there's no  better time than now to take that first  step towards learning that skill you've  always dreamed of having and since it's  completely free to try